  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nShort wave will become a closed low as it moves southeast across the\nregion today into tonight. Inverted surface trough will pivot\nwestward through the area today. This combination will bring showers\nacross the region. A bit thunder is not out of the question. Greater\ncoverage and rainfall amounts will occur across eastern counties.\nSome of the convective allowing guidance are generating a few \nbullseyes of heavier rain. Parameters do not look as favorable for \nheavy rain as earlier in the week. Precipitable water will be 1.2-1.3\ninches and the warm cloud depth is unimpressive. Cannot discount \nlocally heavy rain, but if that occurs, would expect it to be \nisolated.\n\nSystem that moves across the area today will develop into a large cut\noff along the Atlantic coast which will create a block through the\nweekend. Being on the backside of the system, it will be dry and once\nlow clouds clear out on Thursday, mainly clear -- just some high \nclouds Friday and perhaps a bit of diurnal cumulus over the weekend.\n\nHighs will remain cool, and after tonight lows will follow suit.",
